     sseettffssmmaacc — set MAC label for a file hierarchy

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     sseettffssmmaacc [--eehhqqvvxx] [--ff _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e] ... [--ss _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e] ... _f_i_l_e _._._.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The sseettffssmmaacc utility accepts a list of specification files as input and
     sets the MAC labels on the specified file system hierarchies.  Path names
     specified will be visited in order as given on the command line, and each
     tree will be traversed in pre-order.  (Generally, it will not be very
     useful to use relative paths instead of absolute paths.)  Multiple en‐
     tries matching a single file will be combined and applied in a single
     transaction.

     The following options are available:

     --ee      Treat any file systems encountered which do not support MAC la‐
             belling as errors, instead of warning and skipping them.

     --ff _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e
             Apply the specifications in _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e to the specified paths.
             _N_O_T_E_: _O_n_l_y _t_h_e _f_i_r_s_t _e_n_t_r_y _f_o_r _e_a_c_h _f_i_l_e _i_s _a_p_p_l_i_e_d_; _a_l_l _o_t_h_e_r_s
             _a_r_e _d_i_s_r_e_g_a_r_d_e_d _a_n_d _s_i_l_e_n_t_l_y _d_r_o_p_p_e_d_.  Multiple --ff arguments may
             be specified to include multiple specification files.

     --hh      When a symbolic link is encountered, change the label of the link
             rather than the file the link points to.

     --qq      Do not print non-fatal warnings during execution.

     --ss _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e
             Apply the specifications in _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e, but assume the specifica‐
             tion format is compatible with the SELinux _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e format.
             _N_O_T_E_: _O_n_l_y _t_h_e _f_i_r_s_t _e_n_t_r_y _f_o_r _e_a_c_h _f_i_l_e _i_s _a_p_p_l_i_e_d_; _a_l_l _o_t_h_e_r_s
             _a_r_e _d_i_s_r_e_g_a_r_d_e_d _a_n_d _s_i_l_e_n_t_l_y _d_r_o_p_p_e_d_.  The prefix “sebsd/” will
             be automatically prepended to the labels in _s_p_e_c_f_i_l_e.  Labels
             matching “<<none>>” will be explicitly not relabeled.  This per‐
             mits SEBSD to reuse existing SELinux policy specification files.

     --vv      Increase the degree of verbosity.

     --xx      Do not recurse into new file systems when traversing them.

